WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.836
-Welcome back, everybody.
You know it can be hard

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.103
to make big life decisions,
and sometimes

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.538
we could all use a little help.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:09.609
With that in mind, it's time
for "Life Coach with Bill Burr."

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.809
♪♪

00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:16.215
-♪ Life Coach with Bill Burr ♪

00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:18.217
-Wow. I love that.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.820
♪ Life Coach ♪

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.622
I'm joined now
by life coach Bill Burr.

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:25.158
Thank you for being here, Bill.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.326
-That might be the height of
the segment, that little song.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.795
-[ Laughs ] No, no.
So, here's what --

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.429
Let me explain what we did.
We had viewers

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:33.566
send in some questions
that they need your coaching on.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.868
And I'd love for you
to give some tough advice.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.371
-That's right. If you can't
afford a professional,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.105
ask someone with no degree.

00:00:40.105 --> 00:00:41.640
Let's do it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.710
Here we go.
The first one says...

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.022 line:0%
-Well, it's great
that you love your cat

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.257 line:0%
'cause your boyfriend
doesn't love you.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:00:59.525 line:0%
All right?

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.961
If he loved you,
he would have moved in with you.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.729
Or if he loved you
at that level.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:07.333
Like, if I met --
When I met my wife,

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.701
the woman of my dreams,

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.770
if she had a cat
and I was allergic to it,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.873
I would have figured
something out.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.441
I wouldn't have been like,
"Listen. You're the one for me.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:19.879
I think about you all the time.
But you got a cat, so..."

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:23.082
I think he's saying
he enjoys having sex with you

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:25.151
but he doesn't want
to go any further.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.654
So, you know.
-Yeah. Wow.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.355
-I hope you got a nice cat.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:32.325
-There you go. Hey.
Number two...

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.031 line:0%
-Ohh.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.272 line:0%
Yeah.
You don't marry the guy.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.740 line:0%
-Yeah.
-All right?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.575 line:0%
And I don't even think
you're in love with the guy

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.377
you're working with.
-Yeah, me neither.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.078
-I just think --
You're not in love.

00:01:53.078 --> 00:01:54.447
You don't want to do this.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.982
You know what
the problem is, Jimmy?

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.351
Is they never teach you
how to break up with somebody.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.452
Okay? So...

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:02.255
This person has probably wanted

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.390
to get out of this relationship
for -- What would you say?

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.493
At least a year, maybe two?
-Yep.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.662
-So what this person
really needs

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.197
is help on how to break up.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:14.800
So what you gotta do -- All
you say is, "We need to talk."

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.902
And then when he sits down,
just say,

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:18.871
"Look.
I don't want to marry you."

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.873
Just get it out there.

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.641
Now the Band-Aid's
been ripped off.

00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:25.311
And whatever he's going to do,
it's going to crush him.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.946
It's going to break his heart.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:30.883
But it'd be way worse
if you broke his heart

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.853
a couple decades
and a couple of kids from now.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.488
You know?
So just get out of it.

00:02:36.488 --> 00:02:39.325
"I don't want to marry you."
-Yeah. I totally agree.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.362
-Bang that guy at work,
but you don't love him, either.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.198
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:58.611 line:0%
-Stop thinking
that women are so precious.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:01.714 line:0%
All right? They're human beings.
They're just like men.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.283
They make a lot of mistakes,
and they also have faults.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.019
The fact that, like --

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.654
This dynamic
when you get in a relationship

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.356
that women can basically say --

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.325
You know, anything
you need to work on,

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.894
they're gonna bring it up,
but you have to approach it

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.396
like the end of an action movie,

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:20.299
like, which wire can I snip
so this thing doesn't blow up.

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:23.135
You got to sit there
and say, "Listen.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:24.971
You know, I'm not saying
I don't love you.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.638
I'm not saying
I don't care about you.

00:03:26.638 --> 00:03:29.408
But you sound like a dump truck
full of peat moss

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:30.576
backing up every night...

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.011
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:35.181
-...and I can't get to sleep,
so something's gotta give.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:39.718
I don't want you to wear
a scuba mask, you know?

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:42.121
So can I just sleep
in the other room?"

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.089
-Yeah. Or can we get
a Breathe Right strip?

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:45.825
There's things we can do.

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:48.294
-"Your snoring is as ugly
as you are beautiful.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.963
Honey, I have to sleep
down the hall."

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:53.232
This is a great exercise,
though.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.401
Because there's this
whole narrative out there

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.803
that guys are just these A-holes
to their girlfr--

00:03:57.803 --> 00:03:59.238
Like, every one of us.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:02.774
And most guys are like this guy,
where it's, like, you're afraid.

00:04:02.774 --> 00:04:04.911
"Hey, I don't want
to say anything,

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.413
but, you know,
your mom pushed my kid

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.616
down the stairs the other day.
I don't want to offend you."

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:12.618
It's just like --- You just --
You gotta get it out there.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.987
Just say, "Listen. You are..."

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:17.923
If my wife snores,
I just take my foot

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:20.026
and I slowly push her
out of the bed.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.661
-Okay. Here we go.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.729
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:25.965
-She does it to me, too.
She'll just wake me up.

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.434
She'll just be like,
"You got to get out of here."

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.936
-I know. Gosh.
-"Am I snoring?"

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.071
She's like,
"Yes. Get out of here."

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.907
And she, like, hands me
the pillow and the comforter.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:39.545
I don't wake up the next day
upset with her.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.679
-[ Laughs ] No.

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:43.349
-♪ Honesty ♪

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.962 line:0%
-All right, first of all,
you gotta address

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.831 line:0%
the honesty of the situation.
He doesn't keep forgetting.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.400 line:0%
What happens is
you keep washing his dishes.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.137
All right? And you're not
calling him on his [bleep].

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:07.040
So bas-- Oh, sorry. You're not
calling him on his business.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.375
So I would say, you know...

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:11.911
-He forgets to wash them.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.046
-Can you beat this guy up?
Can you beat this guy up?

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:16.182
'Cause if you can,
you can just threaten vi--

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.217
You can use
the threat of violence.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:21.487
"If you don't do this, I'm gonna
beat the [bleep] out of you,"

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:24.223
which for some reason you're not
allowed to say that anymore

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.292
despite when somebody
needs an ass-kicking.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:29.095
So, Jimmy, we got go
more progressive here.

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:30.563
-Yeah. Okay.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:33.699
But leaving dishes in the sink,
this is -- You threaten him?

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.868
-I would just start
scraping the food off his plate

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.804
and put it in his pillow case.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:40.005
But I'd be nice
and I'd leave a Post-It.

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:41.273
I'd say, "Hey, you know,

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.108
you keep forgetting your food
on the plate,

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:44.643
so I figured
I'd put it in a place

00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:46.578
where you'd remember it."

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:49.549
Don't do it and not say
that you did it

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.684
'cause then you're
going to look like some chick

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.952
who keyed his car.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.387
You got to let him know
you did it.

00:05:55.387 --> 00:05:57.189
Then when he comes out,
just be like, "Listen.

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:58.957
I'm not your maid.
And you're not forgetting.

00:05:58.957 --> 00:06:00.659
And I'm not cleaning up
after you.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.895
You do it again,
I'm going to take biggest plate

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.230
I can find
that you used or I used

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:06.832
and I'm gonna smash it
over your head."

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:08.300
And I hate to say that,

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.671
but violence is only thing that
people like that understand.

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:15.374
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:16.642
The threat of violence.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.010
-I want to do this
all night long.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.912
-This could be
my new self-help book.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:23.516
-[ Laughs ] Okay. All right.
This is the last one here.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:25.317
I just figured
I'd say this because you --

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:28.387
-Out of everybody,
that guy bugged me the most.

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:30.990
-Yep. Oh, really? Yeah.
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.025
I lived with a guy like that.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.727
-Yeah. Forget to wash them.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.730
I'm bringing this up because,
gosh, you have a beautiful --

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.166
You have two babies. You have
a beautiful little 4-year-old.

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:42.735 size:88% position:56% line:0%
So this one is -- It says...

00:06:53.011 --> 00:06:54.514 line:0%
-All right.
This is what happens.

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.315 line:0%
Sometimes when you love
your kids so much,

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.817 line:0%
you're afraid
to discipline them,

00:06:57.817 --> 00:06:59.585 line:0%
